{"id":55899,"ord":126,"n_segments":127,"prev":55898,"next":null,"doc":{"id":"68097","title":"68097_Freddie Green oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Freddie Green","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68097/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68097"},"chapter":"The band in 1977","title":"Bobby Plater and Danny Turner in the sax section","category":"person_portrait","summary":"They praise Plater and Turner; at the close Greene says he no longer has to play peacemaker.","period":"1970s","year_from":1970,"year_to":1979,"words":170,"start":[254,6],"end":[255,16],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68097#s55899","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Count Basie Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Count Basie"}]},"people":[{"name":"Danny Turner","qid":null,"n":4},{"name":"Benny Carter","qid":"Q356715","n":1},{"name":"Bobby Plater","qid":"Q4935465","n":1}],"story":{"theme":30,"theme_name":"The reed and horn player's craft: clarinet, sax, tone","community":63,"community_name":"Coleman Hawkins and the great saxophonists","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":254,"b":6,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Bobby's another quiet guy."},{"p":254,"b":7,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Yes."},{"p":254,"b":8,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"I wish he'd take more solos. I like the way he plays."},{"p":254,"b":9,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Yes. He plays beautifully."},{"p":254,"b":10,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"You know, when he -- I mean apart from those ballads, when he --"},{"p":254,"b":11,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Well, no. He can swing too."},{"p":254,"b":12,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yeah. He can sound a bit like Benny Carter."},{"p":254,"b":13,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Right. And, he should. He really should."},{"p":254,"b":14,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"The other guy's quite nice, too. What's his name? The other alto?"},{"p":254,"b":15,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Danny?"},{"p":254,"b":16,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yeah."},{"p":254,"b":17,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Danny Turner? You like him?"},{"p":254,"b":18,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yeah."},{"p":254,"b":19,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Yeah."},{"p":254,"b":20,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"I think he's a little more --"},{"p":254,"b":21,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Modern, yeah."},{"p":255,"b":0,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"-- beboppish but still good."},{"p":255,"b":1,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Yeah. Yeah."},{"p":255,"b":2,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"In fact, that's a good sax section."},{"p":255,"b":3,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Yeah. He's technical."},{"p":255,"b":4,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"He's what?"},{"p":255,"b":5,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Technical."},{"p":255,"b":6,"s":"MRS. DANCE","x":"Technical."},{"p":255,"b":7,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yes. But, still he's got some imagination."},{"p":255,"b":8,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Oh, yes."},{"p":255,"b":9,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yeah. It's very technical."},{"p":255,"b":10,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Yes."},{"p":255,"b":11,"s":"MRS. DANCE","x":"Do you still have to play the peace-maker at any time, in the bus, or anything, or occasionally? Is that a role for you anymore?"},{"p":255,"b":12,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Not really."},{"p":255,"b":13,"s":"MRS. DANCE","x":"No?"},{"p":255,"b":14,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"No."},{"p":255,"b":15,"s":"MRS. DANCE","x":"Maybe guys don't feel so serious about things, or anything."},{"p":255,"b":16,"s":"MR. GREENE","x":"Not really. Not like back in the days --"}]}